+# CLAUDE.md
+
+This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.
+
+## Project Context
+
+This is the **openEuler Linux kernel** source tree, branch `OLK-6.6` (based on upstream Linux 6.6). Origin: `https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel.git`.
+
+It follows the standard Linux kernel layout: core code in `kernel/`, MM in `mm/`, filesystems in `fs/`, networking in `net/`, drivers in `drivers/`, architecture code in `arch/`, public headers in `include/` and `include/uapi/`, build helpers in `scripts/` and `tools/`, and tests in `tools/testing/selftests/` and `lib/kunit/`.
+
+Downstream openEuler patches often carry an `[OLK-6.6]` tag in the subject and an internal reference like `!22417`.
+
+## Build Commands
+
+- `make openeuler_defconfig` — baseline config for openEuler (x86_64)
+- `make x86_64_defconfig` / `make i386_defconfig` — upstream baseline configs
+- `make menuconfig` — interactive configuration
+- `make -j$(nproc)` — build kernel and modules
+- `make -j$(nproc) M=drivers/foo` — build a single driver subtree
+- `make W=1 path/to/file.o` — compile one object with extra warnings
+- `make modules` — build modules only
+- `make modules_install INSTALL_MOD_PATH=/path` — install modules
+- `make clean` / `make mrproper` — clean generated files (`mrproper` also removes `.config`)
+- `make headers_check` — validate exported UAPI headers
+
+Kbuild supports out-of-tree builds via `make O=/build/dir`. If you use `O=`, it must be passed to every `make` invocation.
+
+## Testing Commands
+
+- `./tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run` — run KUnit tests (requires Python, uses UML by default)
+- `./tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py run --kunitconfig=.kunit/.kunitconfig` — run KUnit with custom config
+- `make kselftest` — run kernel selftests
+- `make -C tools/testing/selftests TARGETS=foo` — run one selftest suite
+
+KUnit tests live in `lib/kunit/`. Selftests live in `tools/testing/selftests/<subsystem>/`.
+
+## Style & Patch Checks
+
+- `scripts/checkpatch.pl --strict <patch>` — check patch style before submission
+- `scripts/checkpatch.pl -f path/to/file.c` — check a source file directly
+- Follow `Documentation/process/coding-style.rst`: tabs, 8-column tab stops, kernel brace style, 80-column soft limit.
+- `.clang-format` exists but should only be used on deliberately scoped code, not whole legacy files.
+
+## Commit Conventions
+
+- Use subsystem-prefixed subjects: `iommu/ummu-core: support TID sharing within same mm`
+- Downstream openEuler patches often include `[OLK-6.6]` in the subject
+- Include `Signed-off-by:` when submitting patches
+- Keep the body focused: problem, fix, and validation
+
+## Useful Investigation Commands
+
+- `scripts/get_maintainer.pl -f path/to/file` — find maintainers and mailing lists for a file
+- `git grep -n "symbol_name" -- include/ drivers/` — search headers and drivers
+- `make cscope` / `make tags` — generate indexer files
